# Each word or phrase stands in for a plainer one (`delve into` for
# `read`, `showcase` for `show`, `tapestry` for `mix`) and turns up far
# more in generated text than in docs a person wrote. The Optional rule
# of the same name holds the words that human-written docs also use.
#
# `unlock`, `harness`, `landscape`, `realm`, and `underscore` are left
# out, because each names something in code (a mutex, a test harness,
# a page orientation, a Kerberos realm, the character). The stock
# phrases built on them count instead (`harness the power`, `unlock the
# full potential`, `the landscape of`, `the realm of`), and the
# importance rule holds `underscores the importance`. `elevate
# privileges` names a security operation, so `elevate` skips a
# following `privileges` or `permissions`.
#
# `$foster`, `$showcase`, `$garner`, and `$boast` expand to every form
# of the word through Harper's dictionary. A space in a pattern matches
# only whitespace, so `deep[-, ( )]dive` matches the spaced and the
# hyphenated spelling alike.
expr main [delve, delves, delving, (dive into), (deep[-, ( )]dive), unleash, unleashes, empower, empowers, empowering, streamline, streamlines, streamlined, ([elevate, elevates] ![privilege, privileges, permissions]), tapestry, journey, (navigate the [complexities, complexity, landscape, world, challenges]), testament, $foster, $showcase, $garner, $boast, interplay, intricacies, synergy, (at its core), (at its heart), (at the heart of), (under the hood), nuanced, multifaceted, meticulous, meticulously, bolster, bolsters, bolstered, bolstering, spearhead, spearheads, spearheaded, spearheading, supercharge, supercharges, supercharged, supercharging, revolutionize, revolutionizes, revolutionized, revolutionizing, embark, embarks, embarked, embarking, ([harness, harnesses, harnessing] the power), ([unlock, unlocks, unlocking] the potential), ([unlock, unlocks, unlocking] the [full, true] potential), (the realm of), (landscape of), ([strike, strikes, striking] a balance), (key takeaway), (key takeaways)]
let message "Fancy word. Use the plain word it stands for."
let description "Flags fancy words and phrases, such as delve, showcase, and tapestry, that stand in for a plainer word."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "Unlock releases the mutex."
allows "The test harness builds the fixture once."
allows "The realm names the Kerberos domain."
allows "Names with an underscore are private."
allows "The installer elevates privileges with sudo."
allows "Rotate the page to landscape orientation before printing."
